// Remembers which plots inside it have finished appearing, so a plot that is painted again after a
// gap — a row a virtual list scrolled out of view and back — shows its data whole instead of
// drawing in again.
//
// Wrap the list, or whatever region repaints its plots on and off, in one:
// A plot is remembered by its global element id and its `->appear_generation`, once its appear has
// finished; a new generation still replays it, and one taken away mid-appear draws in again from
// the start. The memory is the scope's own element state: it lasts while the scope is painted
// every frame and goes with it, so a view that is closed, or a scope whose id changes — name it
// after the content, such as a conversation — draws its plots in afresh. The innermost scope wins.
// Without one, every plot draws in each time it is painted anew.
//
